{"y":1979,"label":"1978–79","coach":"Dom Perno","conf":"Ind","confShort":"Ind","w":21,"l":8,"finish":"r32","seed":5,"region":"East","srs":3.19,"sos":-2.37,"ppg":78.7,"oppg":73.1,"story":{"headline":"Two Freshmen Lead UConn Back to the NCAAs","text":"Perno's second season turned on two Connecticut freshmen: Corny Thompson, who had captained Middletown High through a 76-game winning streak, and Bridgeport's Mike McKay. Thompson averaged 18.6 points and 10.0 rebounds, McKay added 15.9 points, and seniors Randy LaVigne and Jeff Carr steadied a team that started 10–2 and went 12–1 at home. UConn won overtime thrillers over Rutgers (69–67) and Holy Cross (109–102, at Boston Garden), then won eight of its last nine regular-season games, capped by an 80–75 overtime win over Rhode Island in New Haven. At the ECAC New England tournament at the Providence Civic Center, the Huskies routed Boston College 91–74 and beat Rhode Island again, 58–50, in the final to earn the program's first NCAA bid since 1976. Thompson was the tournament MVP and swept ECAC and New England Player of the Year and Rookie of the Year honors. Seeded fifth in the East, UConn met fourth-seeded Syracuse in Providence on March 10, 1979. Perno later recalled his team trailing by 18 and closing to two before losing 89–81. The 21 wins were UConn's most since 1964–65.","moments":[{"date":"1979-01-26","title":"109–102 at Boston Garden","text":"UConn outlasts Holy Cross 109–102 in overtime in the Colonial Classic at Boston Garden."},{"date":"1979-03-01","title":"ECAC New England tournament","text":"UConn routs Boston College 91–74 in the opening round of the ECAC New England tournament at the Providence Civic Center, then beats Rhode Island 58–50 in the final for the title and an NCAA bid; Corny Thompson is named tournament MVP."},{"date":"1979-03-10","title":"NCAA Tournament: L vs Syracuse","text":"Fifth-seeded UConn falls 89–81 to fourth-seeded Syracuse in the NCAA East second round at the Providence Civic Center, its first NCAA tournament game since 1976."}],"honors":["ECAC New England tournament champions","Corny Thompson – ECAC tournament MVP","Corny Thompson – ECAC and New England Player of the Year","Corny Thompson – ECAC and New England Rookie of the Year"],"sources":["https://uconnhuskies.com/documents/download/2026/8/13/RECORD_BOOK_26-27_V2_.pdf","https://www.sports-reference.com/cbb/schools/connecticut/men/1979-schedule.html","https://www.sports-reference.com/cbb/postseason/men/1979-ncaa.html","https://archive.org/details/InternationalHeraldTribune1979FranceEnglish","https://uconnhuskies.com/honors/huskies-of-honor/corny-thompson/5","https://web.archive.org/web/20090603182622/http://middletowncthalloffame.com/2006/2006.htm","http://www.uconnhooplegends.com/menslegends/ThompsonCorny.html","http://www.uconnhooplegends.com/menslegends/PernoDom.html"]},"roster":[{"pid":"corny-thompson-1","name":"Corny Thompson","num":"52","cls":"FR","pos":"F","ht":"6-8","wt":225,"home":"Middletown, CT","photo":"assets/players-remote/6282af539dc404.jpg","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":29,"gs":null,"mp":34.2,"pts":18.6,"trb":10.0,"ast":1.8,"stl":1.6,"blk":null,"tov":null,"fg_pct":0.474,"fg3_pct":null,"ft_pct":0.798,"orb":null,"pf":3.4},"tot":{"mp":991,"fg":190,"fga":401,"fg3":null,"fg3a":null,"ft":158,"fta":198,"orb":null,"drb":null,"trb":289,"ast":53,"stl":45,"blk":null,"tov":null,"pf":98,"pts":538,"g":29},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.543,"efg_pct":null,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":null,"ws_per_40":null,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null},"verified":["record_book"]},{"pid":"mike-mckay-1","name":"Mike McKay","num":"5","cls":"FR","pos":"G","ht":"6-5","wt":190,"home":"Bridgeport, CT","photo":"assets/players-remote/274f72964ad523.jpg","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":28,"gs":null,"mp":33.3,"pts":15.9,"trb":5.4,"ast":2.6,"stl":1.0,"blk":null,"tov":null,"fg_pct":0.426,"fg3_pct":null,"ft_pct":0.711,"orb":null,"pf":2.7},"tot":{"mp":933,"fg":169,"fga":397